That's a model selection issue. You'd need to compare the AICs of your candidate models. If it turned out the model with the control covariate was preferred to other models, then yes, you could say that the estimates from that model (like D = 2.21) are the ones that are best supported by your data. Some people prefer to use model averaging in this context, see ?modelAverage.

Ian

